        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-07"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧭 Central Observation\n\nStudy 07 is valuable because it **does not force the ontology to expand very much**.\n\nIts underlying structure is recognizable from Study 01:\n\n- state a strong thesis\n- explain the mechanism\n- develop an illustrative case\n- add historical precedent\n- propose action\n- return to the evidentiary standard\n- close\n\nThe distinctive device is a long **future-scenario simulation** in which Lionel narrates what he imagines the breaking-news cycle would look like if the defendant died before trial.\n\nThat appears to be a rhetorical move inside a thesis monologue, not evidence for an entirely new episode family.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786060285808,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study07-seg1",
      "type": "markdown",
