        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-07"
        },
        "markdown": "# 1 · Warning Thesis\n## 0:00–3:14\n\nLionel opens with the prediction that there may never be a Tyler Robinson trial because Robinson may not survive long enough to reach it. He argues that the disappearance of the defendant would also make unresolved investigative questions easier to abandon. \n\n**Function:** state a high-stakes forecast and immediately explain why the forecast would matter to the larger inquiry.\n\n**Existing move:** `Lionel States Thesis`.\n\n**Possible role:** `warning` or `risk-forecast`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786060285808,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
