        },
        "markdown": "# 5 · Counterfactual Reconciliation Strategy\n## 12:49–15:12\n\nLionel proposes what he would do in Candace's position: approach Erica Kirk, end their public conflict, frame both women as sharing an interest in identifying the real killer, and thereby deprive hostile commentators of the conflict they exploit. \n\n**Function:** move from diagnosis to a hypothetical strategic intervention.\n\nThis resembles Study 04's `Lionel Reconstructs an Answer`, but the target is social strategy rather than a debate response.\n\nA broader reusable role may be:\n\n## `Lionel Proposes a Countermove`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786060285808,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
