        "markdown": "# 7 · Return to the Proof Standard\n## 16:39–19:26\n\nLionel explicitly says that small anomalies are interesting but not the most important issue. He returns to the weapon and argues that unless the rifle can be connected to the shooting, it cannot support guilt. He revives the recurring lint-brush and bazooka analogies to make the point. \n\n**Function:** rank evidence by importance and close the argument on the same proof-oriented standard seen in Studies 02 and 04.\n\n**Existing moves:** `Lionel Audits Evidence`, `Lionel Adds Analogy`, `Lionel Reenacts Proof Test`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786060285808,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
