          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-07"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧪 Two Candidate Moves\n\n## 1. Lionel Runs a Future Scenario\n\nLionel temporarily places the audience in an imagined future and narrates:\n\n- triggering event\n- expected public explanation\n- expected media repetition\n- resulting closure of unresolved questions\n\nThis is structurally similar to a courtroom reenactment, except the simulated environment is the **future news cycle**.\n\n## 2. Lionel Proposes a Countermove\n\nLionel asks what he would do if controlling the situation and proposes an intervention intended to change the trajectory.\n\nObserved here in two domains:\n\n- reconcile Candace and Erica\n- protect Tyler from harm\n\nThese should remain provisional until they recur independently.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786060285808,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study07-compare",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Comparison Across Seven Studies",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1130,
        "y": 520
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 690,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
