      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-07"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🗜️ What Study 07 Says About the Ontology\n\nThe earlier studies kept adding composition structures because the specimens genuinely behaved differently.\n\nStudy 07 does something healthier:\n\n**new content, familiar machinery.**\n\nThe episode can be represented with:\n\n### Composition\n`Thesis Monologue`\n\n### Sequence controller\n`thesis`\n\n### Navigation\n`mostly-linear`\n\n### Existing rhetorical vocabulary\nthesis, analogy, historical precedent, pattern, actor map, evidence audit, proof test, audience direction\n\n### Two provisional roles\nfuture-scenario simulation and countermove proposal\n\nThis suggests we are approaching the correct abstraction level. New transcripts can increasingly add **instances and role values** instead of classes.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786060285808,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study07-confidence",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Confidence and Next Test",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
